From: CHEN Xuan <chenxuan@iscas.ac.cn>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 09:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Preload system OpenMP for openRuyi CPU workers

Include RISC-V in the CPU worker OpenMP setup. openRuyi's Clang-built
PyTorch links the system libomp instead of bundling libgomp. Preload the
same runtime before worker startup so generated GCC kernels and ATen share
thread counts and affinity rather than initializing separate thread pools.

Downstream-only: the fallback follows openRuyi's PyTorch packaging.
References: https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/issues/27369
References: https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/166087
---
--- a/vllm/platforms/cpu.py
+++ b/vllm/platforms/cpu.py
@@ -252,6 +252,7 @@
                 CpuArchEnum.POWERPC,
                 CpuArchEnum.X86,
                 CpuArchEnum.S390X,
+                CpuArchEnum.RISCV,
             )
             and not (
                 "libomp" in ld_preload_str
@@ -279,12 +280,16 @@
                 pytorch_libgomp_so_candidates.extend(
                     glob.glob(os.path.join(torch_libs, "libgomp*.so*"))
                 )
-            if pytorch_libgomp_so_candidates:
-                pytorch_libgomp_so = pytorch_libgomp_so_candidates[0]
-                if ld_preload_str:
-                    ld_preload_str += ":"
-                ld_preload_str += pytorch_libgomp_so
-                os.environ["LD_PRELOAD"] = ld_preload_str
+            # openRuyi's Clang-built PyTorch uses the system LLVM OpenMP.
+            pytorch_openmp_so = (
+                pytorch_libgomp_so_candidates[0]
+                if pytorch_libgomp_so_candidates
+                else "libomp.so"
+            )
+            if ld_preload_str:
+                ld_preload_str += ":"
+            ld_preload_str += pytorch_openmp_so
+            os.environ["LD_PRELOAD"] = ld_preload_str
 
         # LD_PRELOAD libtcmalloc, bundled under vllm/libs to reduce
         # memory allocation overhead
